      "path": "cordis.patch.yml",
      "text": "# dsh-browser-plugin bundle patch — the patch layer this package exports.\n#\n# Loaded by the web profile through an explicit `file://` row inserted from\n# `$DSH_HOME/profiles/web/cordis.patch.yml`, so this file exists mainly for a\n# normal `dsh plugin add` install. A single bare-name row mounts this plugin on\n# the profile root.\n#\n# This plugin publishes no service: it registers the `browser_*` tools into the\n# host-owned `tools` registry, registers its bundled skills, keeps the browser\n# runtime module-private, and serves the live-view routes on the web server.\n# Like the package it replaces, it therefore needs no `isolate` realm.\n#\n# It SUPERSEDES `@try-works/dsh-browser-agent`: both would launch a second\n# Chrome and both would render a browser surface. Install one or the other.\n- insert:\n    - id: dsh-browser-plugin\n      name: 'dsh-browser-plugin'\n"
    }
  ],
